WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:07.790
. Joe Biden has made a major selection to
his cabinet pick for his incoming cabinet.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:13.969
That I wholeheartedly, absolutely think is
a disastrous choice.

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:20.020
And that is the choice of Neera Tanden to
lead OMB, OMB as the Office of Management

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.020
and Budget.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.590
That's a cabinet level position.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:27.179
I believe this is by far Joe Biden's worst
selection.

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:29.640
I like many of Joe Biden's picks.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.650
Alejandro Mayorkas for the Department of Homeland
Security secretary, super interesting.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.010
A good pick, well qualified.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.800
Janet Yellen for Treasury.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.940
We've already talked about her.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.220
I think that's a good pick.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.530
There's a long list of good selections by
Joe Biden and all qualified.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:54.220
But Neera Tanden is a disastrous selection
and is a sign of kowtowing to the worst of

00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:01.510
the worst of the establishment Democratic
Party cronyism that is off-putting and distasteful

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:02.770
and disgusting.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:07.720
Neera Tanden is primarily known as a Hillary
Clinton loyalist.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:13.610
To put it put to put it plainly, a one of
these Democratic elites that helped sink Bernie

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:15.780
back in twenty sixteen.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.450
She's proposed cutting Social Security in
the past.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:24.270
Back in 2010, Neera Tanden was involved in
a Center for American Progress, which is the

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.280
organization.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.310
She ran a proposal to cut Social Security.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:37.210
But not only do I think this is a bad pick
because it is exactly the type of Democratic

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:40.660
Party cronyism that the party should be getting
away from.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:46.050
I also think this is a bad pick because it's
controversial on both sides, with many Republicans

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:52.050
thinking that Neera Tanden is just bonkers
and progressives thinking she's a true centrist

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.540
establishment shill that is the epitome of
the problem of the Democratic Party.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:03.360
So you've got the Berney left furious because
they see this as just a smack in the face.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.030
Her organization regularly going after Bernie,
as I already mentioned.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:12.300
But you've also got right wingers who think
Neera Tanden is nuts.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.819
Republican Senator Lindsey Graham calling
Neera Tanden a, quote, nutjob.

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:24.950
And I don't really care what crazy Republicans
think about Joe Biden's picks, except that

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:31.880
they will have the ability to create real
obstacles for confirmation.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:37.709
And it will be a battle for Joe Biden to get
someone confirmed that much of the left doesn't

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:39.370
like either.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:44.750
Lindsey Graham saying, quote, If you want
to make sure this nutjob Tandan doesn't become

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:50.540
the director of the budget in charge of OMB,
then make sure we win Georgia.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:55.850
So Republicans using this to try to win those
races in Georgia, they may create obstacles

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.140
and it'll be a confirmation battle.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.030
The progressive wing of the Democratic Party
is disgusted and Republicans have already

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:06.410
signaled that they could block confirmation
of Neera Tanden.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.220
The left and right both have problems.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:15.650
This is definitely not in keeping, by the
way, with Joe Biden's Unite the Country theme

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.890
unless he means unite the country against
Neera Tanden.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:20.810
I see no gain from this.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.970
Politically, I see no benefit from.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:28.310
This for a Biden administration, just in terms
of the day to day now, much of the case being

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:33.050
made for Neera Tanden is an identity case.

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:37.660
She grew up in Section eight housing and now
she's going to run the national budget.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.570
OK, but she could run it in a good way or
a bad way.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.470
The fact that she grew up in Section eight
housing doesn't tell us whether she's a good

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.550
or bad pick.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.150
She's the first Indian American in this position.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.430
OK, but is she the right person for it?

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:58.010
And as I've said before, identity can be enlightening
and informative if the person is otherwise

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.010
qualified.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.730
Kamala Harris is a very well qualified person
to be vice president.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.480
She could be president on day one if it were
necessary.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.910
And it's very interesting and inspiring that
she will be the first female president or

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:13.040
vice president ever in history.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.040
That's really interesting.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.040
That's inspiring.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.440
That's relevant.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:21.799
But if she were unqualified, being a woman
wouldn't be a reason to put her in that position.

00:04:21.799 --> 00:04:27.110
And in seeing many of the defenses of Neera
Tanden, so far, I'm seeing experience and

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:31.810
connections mentioned, which means she's an
insider, OK?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:36.120
And I'm seeing identity stories which by themselves
don't do too much for me.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.509
Now, in the meantime, Neera Tanden has been
on a tweet delete rampage, deleting about

00:04:41.509 --> 00:04:47.430
800 tweets, many of them critical of Bernie
Sanders and Elizabeth Warren.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:53.509
So to be clear, I can be against this selection
and be in favor of others.

00:04:53.509 --> 00:04:58.470
Yesterday on a livestream I mentioned I don't
at all like the selection of Neera Tanden.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:02.050
And I started getting emails and messages
from people saying, David, why are you attacking

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:03.050
Joe Biden?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.849
This is not the time to attack Biden.

00:05:04.849 --> 00:05:11.180
Listen, Biden won and he's going to be president
if saying I think Neera Tanden is a bad pick

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.069
while lots of other picks are good.

00:05:14.069 --> 00:05:17.650
And if that counts as attacking Joe Biden,
we're going to have a long four years ahead

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.680
of us, my friends.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:24.469
But I think most of the audience understands
I can dislike this election and like others

00:05:24.469 --> 00:05:28.680
and still believe that voting for Joe Biden
over Donald Trump was the right choice.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.680
As I did.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.629
And as I continue to believe.

00:05:31.629 --> 00:05:32.629
Let me know your thoughts.

00:05:32.629 --> 00:05:33.629
What am I missing?

00:05:33.629 --> 00:05:36.589
Am I misguided in my criticism of Neera Tanden?

00:05:36.589 --> 00:06:52.530
Let me know.

